      "quote": "The Berkshire Eagle, 24 May 2021: \"The turnout was nearly 23 percent of Richmond's 1,245 registered voters.\" The paper gives turnout as a PERCENTAGE, not as a ballot count, so the cast figure here is the total cast on the ballot question the same article prints in full -- 260 yes and 22 no, 282 votes. 282 of 1,245 is 22.65 percent, which is what \"nearly 23 percent\" describes. Treat 282 as the count the source supports, not as a figure the clerk certified."
